<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 1 October, from 331 BCE to 1960.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/darius-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">331 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,695 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexander defeats Darius III at Gaugamela</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> routed the far larger army of the Persian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaugamela">Gaugamela</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. The victory broke Achaemenid power and opened the road to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persepolis">Persepolis</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persepolis">Persepolis</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1814">1814 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Congress of Vienna is due to open formally</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s statesmen had gathered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> to redraw the continent after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s fall, and 1 October was fixed for the Congress's formal opening. Its settlement shaped a balance of power that endured for decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1880">1880 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">146 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Philip Sousa takes charge of the US Marine Band</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 25-year-old John Philip Sousa became leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Marine Band. Over the next twelve years he turned it into a celebrated ensemble and began the career that earned him the name 'The March King'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1890">1890 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">136 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress creates Yosemite National Park</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An Act of Congress established Yosemite National Park in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>'s Sierra <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nevada">Nevada</a>, protecting the high country around the Yosemite Valley. John Muir's campaigning had helped make the case for preservation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1949">1949 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">77 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mao Zedong proclaims the People's Republic of China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">From the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiananmen">Gate of Heavenly Peace</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> proclaimed the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>. Communist victory in the civil war placed the world's most populous country under a new regime.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1957">1957 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">69 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">'In God We Trust' first appears on US paper money</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first US banknotes carrying 'In God We Trust', one-dollar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> certificates, entered circulation. Congress had made the phrase the national motto in 1956, at the height of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> anxieties about 'godless' communism.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1960">1960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nigeria gains independence from Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>'s most populous country, became independent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abubakar-tafawa-balewa">Abubakar Tafawa Balewa</a> as prime minister. It was one of seventeen African states to win independence in 1960, the 'Year of Africa'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a></div></div></li></ol>
